{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}{{ amendment.document_id }} - Contract amendment{% endblock %}
{% macro chrome(page_no, section) %}<div class="topline"></div><header class="head"><div class="brand"><img src="{{ logo_uri }}" alt="Caldova Pharmaceuticals logo"><div><b>Contract amendment</b><span>Caldova Pharmaceuticals / Kristos Pharma</span></div></div><div class="meta">{{ amendment.document_id }}<br>{{ section }} · Page {{ page_no }} of 3</div></header><footer class="footer"><span>Confidential · Controlled contract record</span><span>{{ corpus.fictional_notice }}</span></footer>{% endmacro %}
{% block body %}
<section class="page legal">{{ chrome(1,'Amendment 01') }}<div class="kicker">Amendment to manufacturing services agreement</div><h1>CALD-201 award and supply schedule</h1><div class="grid2" style="margin-top:.22in"><div class="card"><div class="label">Underlying agreement</div><p><b>{{ amendment.agreement_id }}</b></p><p>Effective 09 December 2024</p></div><div class="card"><div class="label">Amendment effective</div><p><b>{{ amendment.effective_date }}</b></p><p>Award reference {{ amendment.award_reference }}</p></div></div><p>This Amendment is entered into by {{ agreement_common.customer_entity }} and Kristos Pharma. Capitalized terms not defined here retain the meaning in the underlying Agreement.</p><h2>1. Recitals</h2><p>A. Caldova issued {{ rfp.document_id }} for technology transfer and commercial manufacture of {{ product.name }}.</p><p>B. Kristos submitted {{ suppliers[1].response_id }} and passed the quality and regulatory gates required by {{ corpus.policy_id }}.</p><p>C. Caldova completed a weighted evaluation and selected Kristos as the best total-value offer, subject to this signed Amendment and the applicable Quality Agreement.</p><h3>Award evaluation</h3><table><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Supplier</th><th>Weighted score</th><th>Year-one total</th><th>Decision</th></tr>{% for item in suppliers|sort(attribute='award_rank') %}<tr><td>{{ item.award_rank }}</td><td>{{ item.name }} ({{ item.vendor_id }})</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(item.weighted_score) }}</td><td>{{ item.year_one_total|money }}</td><td>{{ 'Selected' if item.selected else 'Not selected' }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</table><div class="callout"><b>Selection basis:</b> Kristos combined adequate reserved capacity, satisfactory audit status, no open quality actions, accepted commercial terms, and the lowest evaluated year-one cost.</div></section>
<section class="page legal">{{ chrome(2,'Changed terms') }}<h2>2. Product and commercial schedule</h2><table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Amended commitment</th></tr><tr><td>Product</td><td>{{ product.name }} · {{ product.specification_id }}</td></tr><tr><td>Annual plan</td><td>{{ product.annual_volume|number }} tablets / {{ product.annual_batches }} batches</td></tr><tr><td>Reserved monthly capacity</td><td>{{ suppliers[1].firm_capacity_monthly|number }} tablets</td></tr><tr><td>Released-tablet price</td><td>{{ suppliers[1].unit_price|money }} firm for 12 months</td></tr><tr><td>Technology transfer</td><td>{{ suppliers[1].tech_transfer_fee|money }}</td></tr><tr><td>Safety stock</td><td>{{ suppliers[1].safety_stock_weeks }} weeks after commercial launch</td></tr><tr><td>Approved subcontractor</td><td>Piedmont Analytical Services, compendial microbiology testing only</td></tr></table><h2>3. Amendments</h2><ol>{% for change in amendment.changes %}<li>{{ change }}</li>{% endfor %}</ol><h3>Technology-transfer milestone flow</h3><div class="flow">{% for item in amendment.milestones %}<div class="step"><b>{{ item.payment_pct }}%</b><span>{{ item.name }}<br>{{ item.date }}</span></div>{% endfor %}</div><p><b>Milestone evidence.</b> Each invoice must identify the approved deliverable, approval date, and responsible Caldova owner. Payment does not waive acceptance criteria or quality requirements.</p><div class="callout warning"><b>Capacity control:</b> forecast volumes above 420,000 tablets in a month require written confirmation and do not reduce the four-week safety-stock obligation.</div></section>
<section class="page legal">{{ chrome(3,'Effect and signatures') }}<h2>4. Quality and supply controls</h2><p>Kristos shall not begin engineering, PPQ, or commercial execution until the applicable protocols and quality responsibilities are approved. The Quality Agreement governs deviation notification, OOS investigations, change control, data integrity, batch disposition, complaints, and recalls.</p><p>Piedmont Analytical Services is conditionally approved only for the stated testing scope. Kristos remains fully responsible for subcontracted work, data, investigations, and timely delivery. Any location, method, or scope change requires Caldova's prior written approval.</p><h2>5. Unchanged terms</h2><p>Except as expressly changed by this Amendment, {{ amendment.agreement_id }} remains unchanged and in full force. If a conflict exists, this Amendment controls for {{ product.code }}. The purchase order provides quantities and dates but does not alter prices or quality obligations.</p><h2>6. Approvals</h2><p>The procurement exceeds USD 1,000,000 in anticipated annual commitment when capacity, transfer, and forecast exposure are considered. The executive recommendation and approvals below evidence compliance with {{ corpus.policy_id }}.</p><div class="signature-grid"><div class="signature"><b>For Caldova Pharmaceuticals, Inc.</b><br>Mona Kane · Chief Supply Chain Officer<br>16 November 2026</div><div class="signature"><b>For Kristos Pharma</b><br>Alex Mercer · Chief Commercial Officer<br>16 November 2026</div><div class="signature">Andre Lawson<br>Chief Finance Officer<br>Approved 16 November 2026</div><div class="signature">Charlotte Waltson<br>VP of Procurement<br>Approved 16 November 2026</div></div><p class="notice">Typed names and approvals are fictional demonstration data and do not represent real signatures.</p></section>
{% endblock %}
